From 62ab36f38587a81888eba440577e01b758ea45c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SergiioB <119968745+SergiioB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:31:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] xpu(qwen27): XPU_PROFILE works on --tp 2

Each rank gets its own timestamped event pool and its own kernel-name table, so
rank 1's launches no longer take events from rank 0's single-device pool (the
cause of the hang on two cards). The one-shot TP reduce kernels are profiled
through a TpComm hook. A full pool leaves a launch unprofiled and counts it
instead of draining one rank mid-forward, which could wait on a peer event that
has not been appended yet. The report adds, per rank and kernel, the idle time
on the in-order list right before the kernel (a wait on the peer shows there),
and the drafter's own kernels as (other). Without XPU_PROFILE nothing changes.
---
 zig/src/xpu/dev.zig    | 126 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 zig/src/xpu/qwen27.zig |  27 +++++++--
 zig/src/xpu/tp.zig     |  14 +++--
 3 files changed, 127 insertions(+), 40 deletions(-)

